WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.221 --> 00:00:03.535
Welcome, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.535 --> 00:00:05.037
I appreciate it.
You guys are here.

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:07.306
You guys are --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:11.510
Guys, we are coming to you
after the first NFL game

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.880
of the season,
between the Dallas Cowboys

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.682
and the Tampa Bay buccaneers.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.717
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:21.153
The Buccaneers
are trying to win their

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:24.023
second straight Super Bowl
and Tom Brady's eighth.

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:25.324
-Ooh!

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:27.594
-After that, Brady will have to
make a bold choice

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:30.430
whether or not
to become a thumb-ring guy.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.801
Yep, Brady is the
defending champ at age 44,

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:39.171
and he's actually older than
13 of the coaches in the NFL.

00:00:39.171 --> 00:00:40.439
When they tell him to do
something he's like,

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:43.109
"Don't use that tone
with me, young man."

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.845
That's right -- at 44 years old,

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:49.082
Brady is starting his
22nd season.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.417
At this point, the only thing
in the NFL older than Brady

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.620
is Bill Belichick's sweatshirt.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.657
Jesus.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.158
Did you see that thing?
Look at that.

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:00.326
Oh, my God.
That's been through a couple --

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.327
-Come on!

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:04.497
-That's waxed a few cars,
I think.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.965
Yeah, look at that.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.500
But it was a big match-up,
Dallas and Tampa Bay.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.303
Texas versus Florida.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.471
Fans from both teams were
looking at each other like,

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:15.641
"Thank God we don't live
there right now."

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:17.510
Yeah, the Bucs
are a Super Bowl favorite,

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.213
but, on the flip side,
the Houston Texans only have

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:23.816
a 0.4% chance of winning it all.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.718
The Texans said if
they lose the first few games,

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.019
they're just going to
turn the stadium

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.322
into a pop-up Halloween store.

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:32.225
Oh, and people were
talking about this.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:34.393
Ed Sheeran performed at
the kickoff concert

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:35.829
before tonight's game.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:39.198
But the photo the NFL used to
promote it was a little strange.

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:40.767
Take a look at this.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.235
Yeah.

00:01:44.803 --> 00:01:46.539
I couldn't tell if
they were promoting the game

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:49.442
or a reboot of
"Two and a Half Men."

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.412
Yeah, guys, football is back.

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:56.649
But there's --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.318
There's actually just
one tiny thing

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.952
that's been on my mind
about the NFL,

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:01.587
so I decided to
write a song about it.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:04.123
Now, if you don't mind, Roots,
can I get a beat?

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:06.493
♪♪
[ Rhythmic clapping ]

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:25.845
So, what's up with Raiders owner
Mark Davis' haircut?

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:30.150
Bro!

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:48.034
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.535
I appreciate that. Thank you.

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:51.671
Had to get it off my chest.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.206
Thank you, Roots.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.043
Some business news.

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:59.145
Today, Burger King
made a big announcement

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:02.248
that they're removing
120 artificial ingredients

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.217
from their food.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.919
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.220
That's right.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.889
Now the Whopper is officially
just a pickle slice.

00:03:10.889 --> 00:03:13.158
-Oh.
-That's the Whopper.

00:03:13.158 --> 00:03:15.461
That's the Whopper.
-That's the whole Whopper.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:16.495
-Well, this is pretty cool.

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:18.264
I read that Tesla
just got a patent on

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:22.635
laser windshield wipers
that can zap debris off cars.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.437
Yeah, the laser works
like a charm,

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:27.573
unless you have a cat
riding shotgun.

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:29.642
"Get that!"

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:30.743
Some more business news.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.746
I read that UPS
is hiring 100,000 workers

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.848
for the holiday season.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.483
Working for UPS
should be an easy sell.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.251
I mean, sure, you don't get
to see your family

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:41.220
during the holidays,
but at least you get to drive

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.688
in a doorless car in the winter.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:44.524
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.692
And, finally, I heard about
an Australian man

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:50.530
who set a new world record by
planking for 9 1/2 hours.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.864
-Ooh!

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.733
-He was actually following an
online fitness class,

00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:58.737
and then the screen froze,
but he just kept going.

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:00.239
9 1/2 hours of planking.

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:02.474
At that point, you're not an
athlete -- you're a table.

00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:03.676
We have a great show.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.578
Give it up for The Roots,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.212
-♪ I'm up, I'm out ♪

00:04:07.212 --> 00:04:08.481
♪ I'm moving all about ♪

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:09.515
♪ It's not you again ♪

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.985
♪ Oh, yes, no doubt ♪

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:17.589
♪ Yo, where's my joy,
she at P-A State ♪

00:04:17.589 --> 00:04:19.492
♪ Sunshine, it's time to play ♪

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.427
♪ Play on, playa ♪

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.696
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.698
-What a show
we have for you tonight.

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:28.500
He stars in the new movie
"Vacation Friends."

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.035
It just had the biggest opening

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:32.371
for an original movie
in Hulu history.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:36.009
John Cena is here tonight!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:38.544
John Cena!
-Love him.

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:45.017
-Plus, he's got a brand-new
album out tonight, fresh,

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:46.452
called "Jose."

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.854
J Balvin is here!
-Oh!

00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:51.457
-It's out right now.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:52.558
We're going to talk to him,

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:55.494
and then he's performing
for us in studio!

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:59.098
It is a show!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:01.934
Then, later in the show,
we have an all-new

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.669
"Tonight Show Hashtags,"
everybody.

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:06.071
So, yeah,
it's a big show tonight.

00:05:06.071 --> 00:05:07.907
I'm very excited.

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:10.043
You guys, as I mentioned,
football is back,

00:05:10.043 --> 00:05:11.277
and the first game of the season

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.945
was earlier tonight,
right here on on NBC --

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:15.381
Tampa Bay Buccaneers
versus the Dallas Cowboys.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.116
And, as you know,
at the end of every season,

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:19.652
they give out awards,
like Most Valuable Player.

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:22.421
But they also give out awards
at the start of the season.

00:05:22.421 --> 00:05:23.589
-Oh.
-I'll show you what I mean.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.258
It's time for
"Tonight Show Superlatives."

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:26.892
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:33.099
-♪ "Tonight Show Superlatives" ♪

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:37.069
-Our first player, from the
Bucs, is Rob Gronkowski.

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:38.838
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:42.008
He was voted Most Likely to Yell
"Spring Break!" In September.

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:45.611
And, you know,
it's Spring Break somewhere.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:48.881
Next up, from the Cowboys,
is Leighton Vander Esch.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:52.719
He was voted Most Likely To Have
"Neck Day" At The Gym.

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:55.588
It's neck day, bro.

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:57.590
Can you spot my --
-Spot my neck.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:00.125
-Next up, from the Bucs,
is Vita Vea.

00:06:00.125 --> 00:06:02.027
He was voted Most Likely
To Say His Own Name

00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:03.529
Like The Little Caesar's Guy.

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:04.597
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:05.731
-Vita Vea.
-Vita Vea.

00:06:05.731 --> 00:06:07.666
-Vita Vea.
-Vita Vea.

00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:10.636
-Next up, from the Cowboys,
is CeeDee Lamb.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.471
He was voted Most Likely
To Prank Call

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:14.473
With The Fake Name
"Cee Deez Nuts."

00:06:14.473 --> 00:06:16.508
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.508 --> 00:06:18.277
"Hey, can I have
some pizza for..."

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.046
-Caller I.D.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:23.449
-Next up, from the Bucs,
is Grant Stuard.

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:25.550
He was voted Most Likely To Do
A Touchdown Dance

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:27.553
To Kenny G.'s "Songbird."

00:06:27.553 --> 00:06:29.555
[ Band plays
Kenny G's "Songbird" ]

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:31.591
♪♪

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:37.429
Next up, from the Cowboys,
is DeMarcus Lawrence.

00:06:37.429 --> 00:06:39.031
He was voted Most Likely To Say

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:41.934
"You Better Watch Out, I'm
Wearing My Football Glasses."

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:44.469
[ Applause ]

00:06:44.469 --> 00:06:47.173
Next up, from the Cowboys,
is Connor Williams.

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:49.141
He was voted Most Likely To
Reply, "I Didn't Eat

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:51.510
Any Gummies" To Any Question
You Ask Him.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.280
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.515
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:59.218
Next up, from the Bucs,
we have Leonard Fournette.

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:02.255
He was voted Most Likely
To Have A Magnetic Beard.

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:06.058
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:07.893
Don't sneeze. Don't sneeze.

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:09.762
And, finally,
we have the quarterback

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:11.363
of the Bucs, Tom Brady.

00:07:11.363 --> 00:07:13.799
He was voted Most Likely To Lose
A Super Bowl Ring And Say,

00:07:13.799 --> 00:07:14.833
"Eh, I'll Get A New One."

00:07:14.833 --> 00:07:15.868
There you go.

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.537
Those are your
"NFL Superlatives."

